 "info": {
  "contact": {},
  "description": "# Introduction\n\nWelcome to the Agicap Payment API documentation. **This API is designed to help you**\n\n- import payment files that have been generated using external tools into Agicap.\n- synchronise your beneficiaries from a third party source of truth\n\n### Payment Files overview\n\nPayment files allow you to send payment orders to your banks. They can be used for various purposes, such as paying suppliers, employees, or even requesting debits from clients.\n\n### Use case covered by this API\n\n**Use case 1 : synchronise your beneficiaries with your ERP**\n\n**Agicap provides extensive functionalities to store, manage and secure your beneficiaries, for invoice management, pre accounting and payment purposes. If you prefer to keep your source of truth in a third party tool, and synchronise the data of your beneficiaries from this tool to Agicap, this API provides you endpoints to create, list, edit and delete the beneficiaries of an Agicap entity.**\n\nIn addition to individual CRUD operations, a synchronisation endpoint is available to bulk-upsert your full beneficiary list in a single call. The sync key is the beneficiary identifier in your ERP (`erpId`): if a beneficiary already exists for a given `erpId` it is updated, otherwise a new one is created. Unlike the supplier synchronisation, beneficiaries absent from the payload are not deleted — the sync is purely additive; use the delete endpoint to remove one. The sync endpoint is also how you link a beneficiary to its supplier, via the `supplierErpIds` field.\n\n**Use case 2 : Route your Payment Files to Agicap**\n\nAgicap provides the capability to generate payment files directly within its application. However, if you prefer to generate these files outside of Agicap, this API enables you to route them into Agicap in any standard banking format. Once imported, the files are processed and sent to the bank without any modifications.\n\nSupported Formats: the API supports all standard banking formats in\\_`.xml`\\_and\\_`.txt`\n\n### Prerequisites for Using This API\n\nBefore you can use this API, you need to complete a few setup steps :\n\n1. **Activate the right modules**\n    1. **For routing use case, you need to activate a payment solution on your entity. Contact your Account Manager to activate the appropriate payment solution for your Agicap entities. Note that this API is not compatible with all payment solutions.**\n    2. **For beneficiaries use case, you need to activate a payment solution or our account payable module. Contact your Account Manager to activate the appropriate solution depending on your need.** \n    \n2. **Steps necessary for routing only : set up your payment solution. Work with Agicap’s team to set up your payment solution:**\n    1. **Establish connections with your banks.**\n    2. **Create and link your bank accounts to these connections.**\n    \n### Authentication\n\nTo call this API, you need API credentials with a specific scope. Each route in the Agicap Payment API documentation will specify the required scope.\n\nSteps to obtain the right scope for your credentials:\n1. Generate API Credentials. Follow the\\_[Authentication guidelines](https://api.agicap.com/guides/authentication)\\_to generate your API credentials.\n2. Select the Required Scope. Ensure you select the necessary scope when generating these credentials.\n3. Generate your Access Token. Use the Authentication API to generate your access token. Be sure to specify the required scope in your request.\n4. Use the Authentication Token. Include this authentication token in your requests to the Payment API.\n\nThis documentation aims to guide you through the process of integrating and using the Agicap Payment API effectively. If you have any questions or need further assistance, feel free to reach out to our support team.\n",
  "title": "Payments",
  "version": "v2"
 },
